EvoForge

An interactive artificial-life laboratory where neural agents evolve inside a persistent ecosystem.

Download EvoForge

It includes:

Neural-network-controlled organisms
Heritable genomes and mutation
Crossover between nearby agents
Emergent herbivores, omnivores, and predators
Energy, metabolism, movement costs, aging, and reproduction
Lineage formation, ancestry, dominance, and extinction
Spatial hashing for efficient perception and collisions
Plant growth and nutrient recycling
Day/night environmental pressure
Real-time population telemetry
Interactive zooming, panning, inspection, and agent following
Save/load of complete evolving worlds
CSV experiment export
Deterministic experiment seeds
Headless benchmarking
Five passing automated tests
Run it
unzip evoforge.zip
cd evoforge

python3 -m pip install -e .
evoforge run

For a more chaotic world:

evoforge run \
  --agents 500 \
  --plants 1600 \
  --width 1600 \
  --height 950 \
  --seed 42
Controls
Key	Action
Space	Pause or resume
.	Advance one step
1–5	Change simulation speed
Left click	Inspect an organism
Right click	Spawn a plant
Mouse wheel	Zoom
Middle drag	Pan
F	Follow selected organism
G	Toggle population graph
W	Toggle world wrapping
S	Save the entire world
L	Load the saved world
T	Export telemetry
R	Restart
H	Toggle help

The agents are not assigned fixed behavior. Their decisions come from inherited neural networks. The ecosystem supplies the objective function: survive long enough to reproduce.

That means badly adapted strategies disappear, useful strategies spread, and occasionally something strange emerges that was never explicitly programmed. 
